# Documentation reference

Use this when writing or updating project docs. **When** to update is defined in `task-lifecycle.mdc` and `log-failure.mdc`.

## Doc roles

| Doc | Audience | Content |
|-----|----------|---------|
| `docs/STATUS.md` | Agents | Living task board: completed, in progress, blocked |
| `README.md` | Visitors / you | High-level phase progress (tables, next steps) |
| `docs/history/<component>.md` | Learning | Per-area steps, why, working commands |
| `docs/history/lessons.md` | Learning | Wisdom and gotchas accumulated over time |
| `docs/FAILURES.md` | Debugging | Full failure post-mortems |
| `docs/project-roadmap.md` | Planning | Phase definitions — do not edit unless user asks |

## File map (`docs/history/`)

| Area | File |
|------|------|
| Bootstrap, APIs, remote state | `docs/history/IaC.md` |
| `infra/modules/gke/` | `docs/history/gke.md` |
| Other `infra/modules/<name>/` | `docs/history/<name>.md` |
| `services/<name>/`, `helm/<chart>/` | `docs/history/<name>.md` |
| Short gotchas and experience | `docs/history/lessons.md` |

## History entry format (`docs/history/<component>.md`)

Append a dated section when a meaningful sub-task completes:

```markdown
## YYYY-MM-DD — Short title (e.g. 1.3 GKE dev apply)

**What:** One or two sentences on what was done.

**Why:** Why this step mattered for the platform or learning.

**Commands:**
```bash
# copy-paste commands that actually worked
```
```

Keep numbered **History** sections if the file already uses that style; extend consistently.

## Lessons format (`docs/history/lessons.md`)

For reusable experience (security, provider quirks, non-obvious behavior) — not full failure write-ups:

```markdown
## Area — short topic

> **Note:** One or two sentences. Call out risk or follow-up if relevant.
```

Skip routine fixes and facts obvious from the code. Do not duplicate an existing section — extend it.

## Failure format (`docs/FAILURES.md`)

See `log-failure.mdc` for the required template.

## README vs STATUS

- **STATUS** — precise agent state (bullets, blockers, current step)
- **README** — same progress in table form for a quick public read; update on sub-phase step completion (1.3, 1.4, …), not every tiny commit
